  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing socioecological resilience in BRs and UGGps</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activities under this workplan will support Biosphere Reserves and UGGps to improve their socio-ecological resilience--in particular with reference to the conservation of biological, geological and cultural diversity; climate change and related risks; inclusive and equitable green economic development and implementation of a rights-based approach, including with a focus on indigenous, afrodescendent and women&apos;s rights. Activities will include supporting the LAC UNESCO Climate Change, Risk and Resilience Platform, improving site management in Chile and implementing the IberoMAB Action Framework on implementing the Rights of Indigenous and Afrodescendant Peoples in LAC Biosphere Reserves</narrative>
  </description>
